                          Carpentry

Carpentry turns saved Forestry timber into planks, furniture, and construction
framing. Work in the Kingdom Commons or inside any homestead.

  carpentry list
  carpentry mill [quality] <oak|ash|pine> [amount]
  carpentry craft [quality] <oak|ash|pine> <plan>

Use 'reagents wood' first. One timber mills into two matching planks, and the
species and quality must match through every step. Valid qualities are
standard (omitted), fine, superior, and masterwork. For example:

  carpentry mill pine 1
  carpentry craft pine stool
  carpentry mill fine oak 2
  carpentry craft fine oak chair

Furniture plans:

  Stool         2 planks      0 Carpentry skill
  Chair         3 planks     50 Carpentry skill
  Table         6 planks    100 Carpentry skill
  Bookshelf     8 planks    175 Carpentry skill
  Bed          10 planks    250 Carpentry skill

Inside your own homestead:

  place <furniture>
  homestead furnishings
  remove furniture <id|type>

You must own the homestead and carry the crafted furniture when placing it.
Use a specific name such as 'place pine stool'. Placed furniture is saved with
that room and returns after logout or reboot. Each room holds up to eight
furnishings. 'homestead furnishings' shows stable ids such as furniture_1;
remove by that id or by type. Removing one returns it to inventory or leaves it
on the floor if it is too heavy to carry.

The physical furniture plans are stool, chair, table, bookshelf, and bed.
Decorations such as rugs, lanterns, paintings, blankets, and crockery are room
descriptions rather than crafted objects; represent those with 'homestead
look', 'homestead smell', and 'homestead action'. Remove an old descriptive
placeholder when replacing it with a physical furnishing to avoid duplication.

A Framing Bundle costs five matching planks. Deliver completed bundles to
Brant in the Kingdom Commons:

  deliver framing bundles
  deliver <amount> framing bundles

Post-hut upgrades consume both coins and delivered framing. Use 'homestead
upgrades' for exact requirements and 'homestead status' for current delivery
progress.
